    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1175">

                <pb facs="1188" n="1176" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg1176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.7 Richard Hovey/12–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Huddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-08">December 8,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received December 9—3:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8041. American Interests—Japan. Legation’s 4029, June 23;<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d1175-f1"/> Foreign Office note December 7 states Swiss Legation in
                    Tokyo telegraphs December 5 Japanese Foreign Office declared that thorough
                    investigation concerning torpedoing <hi rendition="#italic">Richard Hovey</hi>
                    has been made but revealed no action corresponding to that outlined in
                    Department’s 2043, June 14.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
